      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Start by maintaining a calm and non-threatening demeanor while speaking softly and slowly. Use active listening techniques, such as mirroring and summarizing, to validate the patient's feelings without necessarily agreeing with their behavior. Offer empathetic statements like, \"I can see you are very frustrated right now.\" Finally, set clear, simple boundaries while offering choices to regain a sense of control.",
